<title>JAPAN: Yaohan says staff agree to bonus delay.</title>
<headline>Yaohan says staff agree to bonus delay.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japanese retailer Yaohan Japan Corp said on Wednesday that the company's labour union, on behalf of employees, has agreed to accept a postponement in payments of summer bonuses for a maximum of one month.</p>
<p>The summer bonus was originally scheduled to be paid out on Wednesday. The company gives bonuses twice a year.</p>
<p>Yaohan Japan is currently restructuring as it seeks to overcome financial difficulties.</p>
<p>The company aims to cut interest-bearing group debt to 90 billion yen from 164.6 billion yen over the next two years through the sale of stores, offices and a portion of its overseas assets.</p>
</text>
